# Ensafely Provider

The Ensafely provider manages a Tenant's configuration in
[Ensafely](https://app.ensafely.com) (cloud): Checks, alert channels,
escalation policies, connections, settings and Probe regions. The standalone
open-source Checker is not supported.

New to the provider? The [getting started guide](guides/getting-started.md)
covers creating an API key, configuring the provider and importing an existing
Tenant with `terraform plan -generate-config-out`.

## Requirements

- **Terraform 1.11 or newer, or OpenTofu 1.11 or newer.** Every secret is a
  [write-only argument](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/resources/ephemeral#write-only-arguments):
  a `<field>_wo` value that never enters plan or state, paired with a
  `<field>_wo_version` number you increase to send a new value. There is no
  `sensitive`-in-state fallback.
- **A Tenant API key** (`ck_...`). Create it in the Ensafely app under
  **Account → API Keys**, with the scope the workflow needs:
  - **API read-write** (`api_write`) to apply changes;
  - **API read-only** (`api_read`) is enough for `terraform plan`, drift
    detection and `terraform plan -generate-config-out`. An apply with it
    fails with **Ensafely request forbidden**.

  Agent keys (created on the Probes page for a Tenant agent) are rejected by
  the API.

